---
import SiteLayout from '../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';
import '../styles/knowledge.css';
const commitments = [
  { title: 'Exercise sound judgment.', text: 'Understand the need, constraints, alternatives and consequences before choosing an approach. Recommend stopping when the case does not justify continuing.' },
  { title: 'Make commitments clear.', text: 'Agree scope, ownership, success criteria, dependencies and delivery expectations. Surface changes early.' },
  { title: 'Ground claims in evidence.', text: 'Distinguish an idea, an experiment, a pilot and a deployed system. Preserve conditions and limitations with reported results.' },
  { title: 'Deliver work others can use.', text: 'Include the implementation, validation, documentation and handover needed for the agreed use.' },
  { title: 'Take responsibility.', text: 'Admit errors, investigate failures, communicate their effect and follow through on the correction.' },
  { title: 'Respect the people affected.', text: 'Account for users, operators, client teams and the consequences of systems acting in the physical world.' },
];
const questions = [
  'Whose problem are we solving, and what outcome matters to them?',
  'What can we credibly deliver, and what still needs to be learned?',
  'What evidence will establish success under the intended conditions?',
  'What obligations will remain after delivery, and who will own them?',
];
---
<SiteLayout title="Our charter — Fidret" description="Fidret's purpose and operating commitments: expertise that earns trust through sound judgment, useful work and reliable delivery." canonical="https://fidret.com/charter/">
  <main id="main" class="knowledge-page charter-page">
    <header class="knowledge-hero shell">
      <p class="section-context">The company charter</p>
      <h1>Trust earned.</h1>
      <div class="knowledge-hero-copy"><p class="knowledge-lead">Build a company whose expertise earns clients’ trust through sound judgment, useful work and reliable delivery.</p><p>Expertise develops through practice. Trust is earned through what people experience when working with us. These commitments set the standard for the company we’re building.</p></div>
    </header>

    <section class="charter-purpose inverse" aria-labelledby="purpose-title"><div class="shell knowledge-split"><div><h2 id="purpose-title">The name carries<br />the intention.</h2></div><div class="knowledge-prose"><p class="knowledge-lead">Fidret means <em>Trust earned.</em></p><p>The name is inspired by the Latin <i lang="la">fīdere</i>: to trust, or to rely upon. It expresses expertise that earns trust, and work people can depend on.</p></div></div></section>

    <section class="charter-commitments shell" aria-labelledby="commitments-title"><div class="knowledge-section-heading"><h2 id="commitments-title">What the purpose<br />asks of us.</h2><p>Commitments guide choices and behavior. They are standards to be held to, rather than a list of outcomes already achieved.</p></div><div class="charter-commitment-list">{commitments.map(item => <article><h3>{item.title}</h3><p>{item.text}</p></article>)}</div></section>

    <section class="charter-questions" aria-labelledby="questions-title"><div class="shell knowledge-split"><div><h2 id="questions-title">Before making<br />a commitment.</h2><p>A decision to narrow the scope, seek a partner or stop can earn trust when the reasoning is clear.</p></div><ul>{questions.map(question => <li>{question}</li>)}</ul></div></section>

    <section class="knowledge-split shell charter-direction" aria-labelledby="direction-title"><div><h2 id="direction-title">The first practice.<br />A broader purpose.</h2></div><div class="knowledge-prose"><p>Physical AI is the first practice to develop. Fidret is the company; practices organize areas of expertise beneath it. A new technology, product or market must serve the same purpose and be justified on its own evidence.</p><p>The starting model combines understanding a client’s situation with hands-on technical work. The first target market, commercial offer and technical approach will be selected through discovery and demonstrated capability.</p><a class="text-link" href="/project/">See how the work connects</a></div></section>

    <aside class="charter-colophon shell"><p>Public presentation of Fidret’s founding direction, established on 24 October 2026. Company commitments and developing practice direction are kept distinct from demonstrated results.</p><a class="text-link" href="/approach/">Read our approach</a></aside>
  </main>
</SiteLayout>
